tree — directory listing utility

This r10 candidate package rebuilds the reviewed Buildroot 2025.02.1 source
recipe from one SHA-256-locked upstream archive.  The payload installs the
real command below /usr/libexec/tdvp-tree and a small /usr/bin/tdvp-tree
frontend. K230 BusyBox already owns /usr/bin/tree, so this explicit alias
never replaces a firmware path.

It requires the exact tdvp-k230-r1 ABI package.  It is not a Debian binary,
and it does not alter firmware, boot, kernel, libc, drivers, or opkg.
